{"kind":"assert","text":"C3 ruling on c5cb1d9c: raise both versions to 0.3.0 and apply.\n\n1. C3 raises Lending and Counter to 0.3.0, each in its typed metadata\n   and in its `dap.application.json`. C3 then applies the two\n   candidate presentation identifiers of c5cb1d9c. Entry, definitions\n   and semantic stay as they are. Grow stays untouched.\n2. The signed 0.2.0 releases do not change. LC-1 keeps their packets\n   and rows. I sign nothing for C3.\n3. The rule from now on, for Lending and Counter:\n   - A version with a signed release never changes its identifiers.\n     The first head that changes an identifier after a signing raises\n     the version to the next minor.\n   - A version with no signed release is open. A later head changes\n     its identifiers and keeps the version. It asks me nothing.\n   - I sign an open version when a request's conditions or an install\n     need the release. The next change then raises the version again.\n   Signed today: Lending 0.2.0 and Counter 0.2.0, per 196d99b7. After\n   LC-1 lands, the packets under `releases/\u003cversion\u003e/` say which\n   versions are signed, and LC-1's test enforces the first line.\n4. R keeps 0.3.0. When R composes on a main that holds C3, it changes\n   the Lending identifiers again under the open 0.3.0, with no second\n   raise. R's stop for my signing decision stands, and I sign 0.3.0\n   after R lands. bdeb6c15 item 1 said that Counter stays 0.2.0. That\n   holds for R alone. C3 raises Counter.\n5. A changed Grow identifier still comes to me before you apply it.\n   The Grow Worker reads its packet from the bundle.\n6. Words. Put the rule of item 3 in one short paragraph where the\n   docs describe `release-identifiers.json`. C3 or LC-1 can carry it.\n   Name the place in your END act.\n\nWhy: the page bundle holds client code, so each client head changes\nboth presentations. A signing for each head would cost a head, a\ngate and a deployment each time. An open version costs nothing.\n\nThe installed 0.2.0 releases serve their own presentation from the\ncontent bucket. Stop and tell me when a reader or a test shows that\na deployment of C3's main changes what an installed 0.2.0 room serves.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}